{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And as for the dream being repeated to Pharaoh twice.</b> That it was repeated two times in a single night — two dreams, yet they were but one dream." "<b>For the thing is established, etc., and Elohim will hasten to do it.</b> And the sage Rabbi Abraham explained that the repetition of the dream in the cows and the ears of grain indicates that 'the thing is established and certain,' but the fact that it occurred twice in a single night indicates that 'Elohim will hasten to do it.' And Rabbenu Hananel, of blessed memory, wrote: 'twice' — this teaches that the first and the second are a single matter; and why twice? 'For the thing is established from Elohim' — this refers to the plenty; 'and Elohim will hasten to do it' — the famine immediately after the plenty."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:21.867693948Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}